course: dictionary
lesson: 12699
title: A doctrine is a set of beliefs or rules
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A doctrine is a set of beliefs or rules that a group teaches or follows. Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «The church teaches a doctrine about forgiveness.» The words church and teaches are clues: a church teaches beliefs, so a doctrine is a belief.
explain: Doctrine can also mean a plan or set of rules that a government, army or group follows. «The government's new doctrine is to protect the forests.» Here the clues are government and protect. Try the swap: "The government's new rule is to protect the forests." It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: In law, a doctrine is a rule or principle that courts follow. «The judge used an old legal doctrine to decide the case.» The clues are judge, legal and case. If the context is not enough, look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: A doctrine is a belief or set of beliefs taught by a church or religion.
fact: The Christian doctrine of the Trinity is one example of a church doctrine.
fact: A doctrine can also be the set of ideas or rules that a government, army or group follows.
fact: In law, a doctrine is a rule or principle that courts follow.
fact: Different churches agree on some doctrines and disagree on others.
exercise: «The church teaches the doctrine that God is loving.» What does doctrine mean here? | A small village in the hills | A kind of weather | A type of musical instrument | *A belief taught by a church
exercise: «The army follows a doctrine of defending its own land.» What is a doctrine here? | *A set of rules an army follows | A song sung by soldiers | A map of the battlefield | A type of uniform
exercise: Jamie says a doctrine is just a fancy word for a hobby. What is the best answer? | Yes, it means a hobby you do on Saturdays | No, it means a loud noise | Yes, it means a school trip | *No, a doctrine is a belief or rule that a group teaches or follows
test: «Different churches agree on some doctrines and disagree on others.» What does this tell you about doctrines? | *Churches can share some beliefs but not all | Churches never talk about beliefs | All churches have exactly the same beliefs | Doctrines are only about food
test: «The court said the doctrine was a rule that judges must follow.» What is a doctrine in this sentence? | A kind of building | *A rule or principle that courts follow | A set of football rules | A short story
exam: In «The government's doctrine was clear: help people in need», which clue shows that doctrine means a plan or set of rules? | There is no clue, you can only guess | *The words help people in need, which show what the government plans to do | The word was | The word clear
